/dev/sda=94.  I also tried with /dev/sda1, since that should be the =
first
partition on sda, with the same result.  Is there another command that
releases the disk for formatting?

=20

Are there any good primers on using FDISK?  Everything I read says this
is for EXPERTS ONLY, so what am I doing here?  Is there a better way to
set up these partitions?

=20

Jim

